cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis pipeline or reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "MTT Assay Analysis: MG-63 Osteoblast Viability on TiO2/Sr Electrospun-Coated 316L Stainless Steel"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rofoee"
    given-names: "Shahrzad"
date-released: 2026-07-12
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shahrzad-Rofoee/mtt-mg63-viability-analysis"
abstract: >
  A reproducible Python statistical analysis pipeline (descriptive statistics,
  Shapiro-Wilk normality testing, Levene's test, one-way ANOVA, Tukey HSD
  post-hoc comparisons, and proliferation t-tests) applied to original MTT
  cytocompatibility assay data measuring MG-63 osteoblast-like cell viability
  on 316L stainless steel coated with electrospun TiO2 and strontium-doped
  TiO2 nanofibers (single-nozzle and dual-nozzle configurations), generated
  as part of M.Sc. thesis research on orthopedic implant surface
  modification.
keywords:
  - MTT assay
  - cell viability
  - MG-63
  - TiO2 nanofibers
  - strontium doping
  - electrospinning
  - 316L stainless steel
  - orthopedic implants
  - biomaterials